# QuantSim -- Docker build context.
#
# Deny-by-default, then name what the builds actually need. The usual shape is
# the other way round (list what to exclude), and it fails open: anything new
# at the repo root is in the context until somebody remembers to add a line.
# This repo is public and the thing most worth keeping out of an image layer is
# .env, so the default is "not included" and additions are deliberate.
#
# Two entries below are load-bearing rather than tidy:
#
#   .env       -- credentials. A `COPY . .` in any future Dockerfile would bake
#                 them into a layer that survives deleting the file.
#   go.work    -- with it present, the build silently uses the workspace, and
#                 the image builds fine while `GOWORK=off go build ./...` is the
#                 only thing keeping a clean clone honest. The builder also sets
#                 GOWORK=off, because this file can be loosened by accident and
#                 that environment variable cannot.
#
# Neither is re-included below. Do not add them.

*

!pkg/
!services/
!frontend/
!infra/docker/

# Inside what we did include.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
